   277	### 1.4 What did not work
   278	
   279	Stated plainly, because the failures cost more engineering time than the wins:
   280	
   281	- **Hybrid never pulled ahead of SVM** despite compiling a bespoke kernel per
   282	  circuit. Per-circuit compilation is not, by itself, a performance strategy.
   283	- **V1 (MLIR) was 5–60× *slower* than SVM.** Full unrolling of the operand
   284	  sequence produced 20 MB of IR, 115 KB/thread of spill scratch [unverified,
   285	  see §5.5], and 221-second compiles.
   286	- **Straight-lining noise operations does not help.** Measured gain: 1.10× on
   287	  instruction count, 1.02× on VALU, and **zero** VGPR relief — 56 in both forms
   288	  (§7.9).
   289	- **MFMA is inapplicable.** `SQ_INSTS_MFMA = 0.0` on **all 52** backend×circuit
   290	  cells of job 50793 — 26 circuits × 2 backends, none missing. (An earlier draft
   291	  could only claim 51 of 52, because `qv24_L4_seed42`'s SVM counter block was
   292	  absent from the truncated job 50785 and was recorded as *unmeasured* rather
   293	  than assumed zero. It is now measured, and it is zero.)
   294	  The workload is a butterfly reduction over amplitudes, not a GEMM.
   295	  Any claim that the matrix cores can be brought to bear here is unsupported by
   296	  this corpus. (§14.6)
