  2551	### 7.9 S7 — the noise runtime loop (the negative result)
  2552	
  2553	**The op** (`v2_ops_body.inc:438-451`):
  2554	
  2555	```c
  2556	static inline V2_NOISE_ATTR void v2_op_noise_block(V2State* st, const CV2NoiseSite* sites, const CV2Channel* channels,
  2557	                                     const double* hazards, u32 num_sites, u32 start, u32 count) {
  2558	    u32 t = v2_tid();
  2559	    if (IS_OWNER) {
  2560	        u32 end = start + count;
  2561	        while (st->next_noise >= start && st->next_noise < end) {
  2562	            u32 site_idx = st->next_noise;
  2563	            apply_noise_site(st, sites, channels, site_idx);
  2564	            st->next_noise = site_idx + 1u;
  2565	            draw_next_noise(st, hazards, num_sites);
  2566	        }
  2567	    }
  2568	    v2_barrier();
  2569	}
  2570	```
  2571	
  2572	`OP_NOISE_BLOCK` covers the half-open site range `[start, start+count)`, but it
  2573	**consumes only those sites the PRNG selects**. `draw_next_noise` performs an
  2574	`ocml_log_f64` hazard draw and advances `st->next_noise` by a random amount. The
  2575	loop's trip count is a function of the random stream. It stays a loop in **both**
  2576	forms; specialization folds only `start` and `count`.
  2577	
  2578	**The two forms** (`cases/S7_noise_block.c`):
  2579	
  2580	```c
  2581	#if SPEC_FORM
  2582	    v2_op_noise_block(st, noise_sites, noise_channels, noise_hazards, num_noise_sites, 131u, 57u);
  2583	    v2_op_noise(st, noise_sites, noise_channels, noise_hazards, num_noise_sites, 188u);
  2584	#else
  2585	    v2_op_noise_block(st, ..., i0.a, i0.b);
  2586	    v2_op_noise(st, ..., i1.a);
  2587	#endif
  2588	```
  2589	
  2590	**Result: 447→407 instructions (1.10×), VALU 214→210 (1.02×), branches 23→20,
  2591	VGPR 56→56, SGPR 86→85.** This is essentially nothing — and the register
  2592	columns, which an earlier draft misreported as `0→0` because LLVM prints them
  2593	symbolically for kernels that call external functions (see the note in §7.2),
  2594	say something stronger than "no gain": **specialization does not reduce this
  2595	op's register pressure at all.** 56 VGPRs in both forms. That matters for §11.1,
  2596	because register pressure is precisely the cost that straight-lining hundreds of
  2597	these into one function *adds*.
  2598	
  2599	The assembly diff confirms it — what changed is only the range test
  2600	(`interp:11-38` vs `spec:15-25`):
  2601	
  2602	```diff
