  3093	
  3094	```asm
  3095	v2_op_noise_block:                      ; @v2_op_noise_block
  3096		s_mov_b32 s33, s32
  3097		scratch_store_dword off, v63, s33 offset:68 ; 4-byte Folded Spill
  3098		scratch_store_dword off, v40, s33 offset:64 ; 4-byte Folded Spill
  3099		scratch_store_dword off, v41, s33 offset:60 ; 4-byte Folded Spill
  3100		... 15 more spills ...
  3101	```
  3102	
  3103	`v2_op_noise_block` is emitted `noinline` (§7.9, §11.1), so it is a real
  3104	function with a real prologue, and a callee-saved register spill sequence. That
  3105	is the price of the FP-scheduling fence. It shows up in the `circuit_d3` ISA
  3106	census as 406 `scratch_store_dwordx2` + 303 `scratch_store_dwordx4`, and it is
  3107	one of the two reasons V2's register-tier ScratchSize is 928 bytes where V1's
  3108	was 156 (the other being the shot-packed register layout of §9.1). §11 returns
  3109	to whether that trade is worth it — the short answer, from the gate results, is
  3110	that it is, because the alternative is a correctness failure rather than a
  3111	slower kernel.
