  3299	### 8.7 What the two pipelines' diffs collectively show
  3300	
  3301	| | V1 | V2 |
  3302	|---|---|---|
  3303	| Where the representation is largest | at emission (23,002 lines, human-authored) | at `-O0` (19,551 lines, compiler-authored, thrown away) |
  3304	| What the "MLIR stage" contributed | constant dedup + CSE; one pass a no-op | n/a — no MLIR |
  3305	| Where `alloca`s die | LLVM `-O2`, and only on small circuits | clang `-O2`, 2,271 → **3** (99.87 %); the 3 are a fixed per-kernel residue, not circuit-scaling |
  3306	| Whether the optimizer stays enabled | no — detuned by IR size above threshold | yes — IR never gets large enough to matter |
  3307	| Vectorization | none — 0 packed ops, with or without the log inlining | 459 `shufflevector` → 431 `v_pk_add_f32`, 416 `v_pk_mul_f32` |
  3308	| `log()` | hand-written in MLIR, re-inlined 54× by `opt` | `__ocml_log_f64`, one call, three relocations |
  3309	| f64 instructions, `circuit_d3` | 4,347 — **68 % of it inlined log** | 187 |
  3310	| Final ISA, `circuit_d3` | 17,802 lines | **10,398 lines** |
  3311	| Compile time, `circuit_d3` | 3.58 s | **2.04 s** |
  3312	| Compile time, `surface_d7_t19` | **221.48 s** | (V2 emits the same circuit in ~4,346 C lines; see §9) |
  3313	
  3314	The single sentence version: **V1 asked the compiler to clean up after the
  3315	emitter, and past a certain size the compiler declined. V2 gave the compiler
  3316	something it was already good at.**
