  3319	
  3320	## 9. Optimizations, tier by tier
  3321	
  3322	V2 did not arrive at its current numbers by specializing. Specialization was
  3323	the fifth thing that happened, and if it had been the first, most of the
  3324	speedup would have been invisible — the earliest V2 build was **28× slower than
  3325	SVM** on `frame_h`, and no amount of constant folding closes a 28× gap.
  3326	
  3327	This chapter walks the optimization history with the progressive ratio table as
  3328	the spine. Every row of that table is a real benchmark run archived under
  3329	`V2_performance/runs/`; the full progression is in
  3330	`V2_performance/analysis/TRENDS.md`.
  3331	
  3332	The sections are ordered by *magnitude*, not by date, and the two differ. The
  3333	actual commit order on `mlir-v2`, from `git log --reverse`, is:
  3334	
  3335	| # | commit | time | what |
  3336	|---|---|---|---|
  3337	| 1 | `d873997` | 07-25 04:46 | P1a — shrink reduction LDS |
  3338	| 2 | `7802423` | 07-25 04:50 | P1b — bit-pack `lds_meas` |
  3339	| 3 | `715f8d0` | 07-25 05:11 | **P0 — shot-packed register tier** |
  3340	| 4 | `eea6e13` | 07-25 07:36 | specializer Phase 1 — operand library |
  3341	| 5 | `b31b400` | 07-25 07:47 | specializer Phase 2+3 — register emitter |
  3342	| 6 | `60d5728` | 07-25 08:24 | specializer — coop tier + correctness gate |
  3343	| 7 | `4b55871` | 07-25 08:34 | force-inline `v2_op_*` in the interpreter |
  3344	| 8 | `9d9cc68` | 07-25 16:24 | noise/measurement `noinline` fencing |
  3345	| 9 | `bbb5e42` | 07-25 16:35 | gate: multi-seed + disk cache |
  3346	| 10 | `5d10409` | 07-25 17:18 | specializer — global tier |
  3347	| 11 | `842d646` | 07-25 23:06 | XOR observable parity |
  3348	| 12 | `150d09f` | 07-26 06:33 | `v2_barrier` → memory barrier |
  3349	
  3350	**P1 shipped 25 minutes before P0**, despite being numbered after it and being
  3351	worth ~10 % against P0's 28×. It was picked first because it was judged the
  3352	safest change in the plan (layout only, no algorithm change), which is a
  3353	reasonable way to start and a misleading way to report — so the ordering is
  3354	stated here rather than smoothed over.
  3355	
  3356	### 9.1 The progression
  3357	
  3358	V2/SVM kernel-time ratio, lower is better, `< 1` means V2 wins. Seven of the
  3359	twelve archived runs, chosen at the points where something changed. Column 5 is
  3360	included **because it regressed** — see the note below it:
  3361	
  3362	| circuit | baseline | after P0+P1 | after specializer | *fenced+gated* | noise-specialized | global-specialized | **final** |
  3363	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
  3364	| frame_h | **28.258** | 1.215 | 0.612 | *2.859* | 0.614 | 0.645 | **0.626** |
  3365	| circuit_d3_p0.001 | 15.193 | 1.081 | 1.116 | *2.117* | 0.524 | 0.504 | **0.525** |
  3366	| qv10 | 1.313 | 1.237 | **0.252** | *0.675* | 0.308 | 0.310 | **0.310** |
  3367	| surface_d7_t15 | 1.650 | 1.469 | 1.787 | *1.427* | **0.503** | 0.507 | **0.505** |
  3368	| surface_d9_t10 | 1.642 | 1.473 | 1.796 | *1.402* | **0.484** | 0.481 | **0.481** |
  3369	| surface_d7_t19 | 0.968 | 0.872 | 1.014 | 1.017 | 1.015 | **0.312** | **0.298** |
  3370	| surface_d9_t19 | 0.906 | 0.817 | 0.973 | 0.971 | 0.972 | **0.262** | **0.262** |
  3371	| surface_d11_t15 | 0.938 | 0.854 | 1.005 | 1.005 | 1.005 | **0.259** | **0.256** |
  3372	
  3373	Read the bolded cells: **each tier's win arrives in exactly one step, and does
  3374	not move afterwards.** That is the signature of a structural change rather than
  3375	a tuning change. Register tier lands at P0. Coop lands at the specializer.
  3376	Noise-heavy coop lands at the noise fence. Global lands at the global emitter.
  3377	
  3378	That reading does not have to be taken on trust. Every archived run kept its
  3379	`rocprofv3` kernel trace, and the kernel *name* in the trace says which code
