  3461	### 9.2 P0 — the shot-packed register tier (28.3× → 1.2×)
  3462	
  3463	**The problem.** The first V2 was a single kernel topology: 256 threads
  3464	cooperate on one shot, amplitudes in LDS, `s_barrier` between every op. That is
  3465	the right shape for rank 10. For `frame_h` — rank 0, four instructions, no
  3466	amplitudes worth speaking of — it means 256 threads doing the work of one, with
  3467	a barrier after each of four instructions, while SVM's register path runs one
  3468	shot per thread. Hence 28.258×.
  3469	
  3470	**The fix** (`715f8d0`). Rather than write a second kernel, the shared
  3471	`execute_shot` body was parameterized on *how threads cooperate*, through five
  3472	macros:
  3473	
  3474	```c
  3475	#ifdef V2_REGISTER
  3476	#  define V2_STRIDE 1u
  3477	   static inline u32 v2_tid(void)  { return 0u; }
  3478	#  define IS_OWNER 1
  3479	   /* v2_barrier() -> nothing; V2_REDUCE2 -> identity (a stride-1 loop already summed) */
  3480	#else
  3481	#  define V2_STRIDE 256u
  3482	   static inline u32 v2_tid(void)  { return __builtin_amdgcn_workitem_id_x(); }
  3483	#  define IS_OWNER (t == 0)
  3484	   /* v2_barrier() -> fenced s_barrier; V2_REDUCE2 -> coop_reduce2 butterfly */
  3485	#endif
  3486	```
  3487	
  3488	**The same opcode arithmetic now compiles two ways from one source.** Under
  3489	`-DV2_REGISTER`, `for (u64 i = t; i < iters; i += V2_STRIDE)` becomes
  3490	`for (i = 0; i < iters; i += 1)` — a plain serial loop in one thread — the
  3491	barriers vanish, `IS_OWNER` is constant-true so the tid0 guards evaporate, and
  3492	the reduction is the identity because a stride-1 loop has already summed
  3493	everything. `GpuComplex v[16]` lives in VGPRs.
  3494	
  3495	The commit's measured result, quoted verbatim:
  3496	
  3497	> Clean kernel-time vs GPU-SVM: frame_h 30.6x→1.14x, circuit_d3 14.1x→1.13x.
  3498	> The 15-28x low-rank catastrophe is eliminated; V2 register tier is now at the
  3499	> 1-shot-per-thread floor (SVM's own topology). Byte-exact vs SVM: 38/38.
