  5151	
  5152	## 14. Performance evaluation: V2 against SVM
  5153	
  5154	Everything to this point has been mechanism — what the specializer folds, what
  5155	the compiler does with it, what an individual opcode costs. This chapter is the
  5156	end-to-end evaluation: 26 circuits, both backends, hardware counters, and an
  5157	attempt to answer the only question that matters — *where does the time actually
  5158	go, and why is V2 faster?*
  5159	
  5160	### 14.1 Method
  5161	
  5162	One SLURM job, **50793**, on one node.
  5163	
  5164	| | |
  5165	|---|---|
  5166	| run | `20260727T125310Z_report-final-allfixtures` |
  5167	| node | `smci350-rck-g03-d13-21` (`mi350x-es`, gfx950) |
  5168	| commit | `79d4463`, working tree clean |
  5169	| circuits | 26, all paired (V2 + SVM), **zero `rocprofv3` aborts** |
  5170	| metric | **GPU kernel time**, `per_dispatch_ns_median` from `rocprofv3` |
  5171	
  5172	Counters are collected in **three separate profiling passes**, because the
  5173	hardware cannot capture them all simultaneously:
  5174	
  5175	| pass | counters |
  5176	|---|---|
  5177	| `pmcA` | `SQ_INSTS_{VALU,SALU,LDS,MFMA}`, `SQ_WAVES` |
  5178	| `pmcB` | `TCC_HIT_sum`, `TCC_MISS_sum` |
  5179	| `pmcC` | `GRBM_GUI_ACTIVE`, `SQ_BUSY_CYCLES`, `SQ_WAIT_INST_LDS`, `SQ_WAVE_CYCLES` |
  5180	
  5181	Each pass is a **separate execution of the kernel**. Counters from the same pass
  5182	may be combined freely; counters from different passes may not be divided into
  5183	each other without an argument that both executions did the same work. §14.5
  5184	turns on exactly this point, and an earlier draft of this chapter got it wrong.
  5185	
  5186	Three further methodological commitments, each learned the hard way and each now
  5187	enforced rather than merely intended:
  5188	
  5189	1. **Kernel time, not host wall time.** The host path differs between the two
  5190	   backends (§13 is entirely about that difference), so wall time would measure
  5191	   the dispatch mechanism rather than the generated code. Where dispatch
  5192	   overhead is the subject, §13 measures it directly.
  5193	2. **Both arms in one job on one node.** `mi350x-es` is heterogeneous;
  5194	   `node.json` in every run directory carries the warning `"Do NOT compare
  5195	   ratios across nodes."` §1.3(d) records what happens when this is violated —
  5196	   a projection off by 2×, in the flattering direction.
  5197	3. **The denominator is checked against the expected denominator.** Job 50785
  5198	   reported `wins 18/18` over a 26-circuit corpus because eight fixture paths
  5199	   had gone stale and `rocprofv3` aborted on each. `bench_all.sh:131-138` now
  5200	   aborts the run rather than continuing past a missing input:
  5201	
  5202	   ```bash
  5203	   # Fail loudly on a stale fixture path. Job 50785 lost 8 of 26 circuits to
  5204	   # renamed fixtures: rocprofv3 aborted on every pass, stderr went to
  5205	   # /dev/null, and the summary reported "wins 18/18" over a silently
  5206	   # truncated corpus. A missing input must not look like a clean result.
  5207	   if [ ! -f "$c" ]; then
  5208	     echo "  *** FIXTURE MISSING: $c -- aborting run ***" >&2
  5209	     exit 1
  5210	   fi
  5211	   ```
  5212	
  5213	   That truncation was not a wash: the six dropped QV circuits are the corpus's
  5214	   *weakest* wins, so their absence moved the median from 0.670 to 0.518. A
  5215	   silent loss of data flattered the result by 23 %.
  5216	
