  5526	## 15. The full benchmark report
  5527	
  5528	§14 argued a thesis. This chapter is the underlying data, in full, with no
  5529	selection: 26 circuits, both backends, every counter collected, every launch
  5530	parameter recorded. **Where any earlier chapter of this report disagrees with a
  5531	number here, this chapter is correct.** §1–§10 were written against earlier runs
  5532	on a different node; several of their figures have been superseded and are
  5533	retained only where the text says so explicitly.
  5534	
  5535	### 15.1 Provenance
  5536	
  5537	```json
  5538	{ "run_id":  "20260727T125310Z_report-final-allfixtures",
  5539	  "label":   "report-final-allfixtures",
  5540	  "commit":  "79d4463",
  5541	  "branch":  "mlir-v2",
  5542	  "dirty":   false,
  5543	  "v2_specialize": true,
  5544	  "n_circuits":    26 }
  5545	
  5546	{ "slurm_job_id": 50793,
  5547	  "node":         "smci350-rck-g03-d13-21",
  5548	  "partition":    "mi350x-es",
  5549	  "arch":         "gfx950",
  5550	  "note": "mi350x-es is heterogeneous. Do NOT compare ratios across nodes." }
  5551	```
  5552	
  5553	> **The node caveat, stated once and meant throughout.** This job ran on
  5554	> `d13-21`. The absolute timings in §1–§10 come from `f13-21`. V2/SVM *ratios*
  5555	> within this job are sound — both arms, same job, same node, interleaved. The
  5556	> absolute microsecond figures must not be compared against those chapters.
  5557	> §1.3(d) is the record of what happens when this rule is broken: a projected
  5558	> ratio of ~0.40 for the d5 family against a measured 0.84, wrong by 2× in the
  5559	> flattering direction.
  5560	
  5561	`v2_specialize: true` is not decoration. `V2_SPECIALIZE` is opt-in; with it
  5562	unset the harness measures the *interpreter*, and the resulting numbers look
  5563	like a 2–3× regression that is really a configuration error. The manifest
  5564	records the flag so a reader can tell which kernel was measured.
  5565	
  5566	### 15.2 What each run does
  5567	
  5568	Per circuit, per backend, five `rocprofv3` invocations — plus one untraced warm-up
  5569	whose purpose is to move `.hsaco` compilation and gating *off* the traced path:
  5570	
  5571	```bash
  5572	prof() {  # $1=outdir  rest=cmd
  5573	  local outdir="$1"; shift; local cmd="$*"
  5574	  mkdir -p "$outdir"
  5575	  eval "$cmd" >/dev/null 2>&1   # warm: compile+gate the .hsaco OFF the traced path
  5576	  timeout 300 rocprofv3 --kernel-trace   --stats --output-format csv -d "$outdir/kt"   -- $cmd
  5577	  timeout 300 rocprofv3 --hsa-core-trace --stats --output-format csv -d "$outdir/hsa"  -- $cmd
  5578	  timeout 300 rocprofv3 --pmc $PMC_A --output-format csv -d "$outdir/pmcA" -- $cmd
  5579	  timeout 300 rocprofv3 --pmc $PMC_B --output-format csv -d "$outdir/pmcB" -- $cmd
  5580	  timeout 300 rocprofv3 --pmc $PMC_C --output-format csv -d "$outdir/pmcC" -- $cmd
  5581	}
  5582	```
  5583	
  5584	The counters are split into three groups because the hardware cannot collect
  5585	them simultaneously (`bench_all.sh:81-83`):
  5586	
  5587	```bash
  5588	PMC_A="SQ_WAVES,SQ_INSTS_VALU,SQ_INSTS_MFMA,SQ_INSTS_SALU,SQ_INSTS_LDS"
  5589	PMC_B="TCC_HIT_sum,TCC_MISS_sum"
  5590	PMC_C="SQ_BUSY_CYCLES,GRBM_GUI_ACTIVE,SQ_WAIT_INST_LDS,SQ_WAVE_CYCLES"
  5591	```
  5592	
  5593	**Each group is a separate execution of the kernel.** Ratios *within* a group,
  5594	and ratios of one counter *between the two backends*, are sound. Quotients of
  5595	counters drawn from *different* groups are not, absent an argument that the runs
  5596	did identical work — §14.5 retracts a claim that violated exactly this.
  5597	
  5598	Shot counts vary by circuit, from 20,000 on the small register-tier fixtures
  5599	down to 500 on `qv24_L4`, chosen so that each run completes inside the 300 s
  5600	`timeout` (`bench_all.sh:90-113`). Shot count therefore differs *between*
  5601	circuits but is identical between the two backends of any one circuit, which is
  5602	what the ratio requires.
  5603	
