  5660	> not the backend. The per-circuit ratios above are the result.
  5661	
  5662	### 15.4 Tier assignment
  5663	
  5664	Tier is a function of `peak_rank` alone (`v2_kernel.cc:312-321`):
  5665	
  5666	```cpp
  5667	constexpr uint32_t kRegMaxRank  = 4;
  5668	constexpr uint32_t kCoopMaxRank = 10;
  5669	const Tier tier = flat.peak_rank <= kRegMaxRank  ? REG
  5670	                : flat.peak_rank <= kCoopMaxRank ? COOP : GLOBAL;
  5671	```
  5672	
  5673	This is worth stating because the fixture names actively mislead. Within the
  5674	surface family, `surface_d11_t10` runs **coop** while `surface_d11_t15` and
  5675	`surface_d11_t19` run **global** — same code distance, different tier — and
  5676	`surface_d7_t5` runs on the **register** tier despite its name suggesting kinship
  5677	with the other `surface_d7_*` circuits. The name encodes the circuit's
  5678	construction; the tier follows from the peak rank the StatevectorSqueeze pass
  5679	leaves behind. **Read the measured LDS size, not the fixture name.**
  5680	
