  5701	Three observations, all structural:
  5702	
  5703	- **LDS.** V2's coop kernels declare `lds_v[1024]` + `lds_red_scratch[512]` at
  5704	  8 B each = 12,288 B, plus `lds_red0`/`lds_red1` (128 B) and `lds_state` —
  5705	  13,064 B in the ELF, which the profiler reports as 13,312 (see below). The
  5706	  global kernels declare neither amplitude array, because at rank > 10 the
  5707	  amplitudes live in HBM; their ELF figure is 784 B of `lds_state` and
  5708	  `lds_shot` (`v2_specializer.cc:185-186`, `:204-205`), reported as 1,024. SVM
  5709	  provisions 23,040 / 8,704 B for the same tiers. The 8.5× global-tier gap is a
  5710	  consequence of where the amplitudes live, not of tuning.
  5711	
  5712	  > `rocprofv3` reports `LDS_Block_Size` **rounded up to a 256-byte granule**:
  5713	  > 13,064 → 13,312 and 784 → 1,024. The ELF `.group_segment_fixed_size` is the
  5714	  > declared size; the profiler figure is the dispatch allocation. This table
  5715	  > quotes the profiler throughout, for consistency with its other columns.
  5716	- **Scratch, register tier.** 656–1,040 B against SVM's uniform 4,480 B — 4.3×.
  5717	  SVM must provision for the worst opcode it *might* interpret; V2 provisions for
  5718	  the opcodes the circuit actually contains.
  5719	- **VGPRs.** V2 uses fewer than SVM on five circuits (32, 32, 36, 52, 52/56) and
  5720	  the same 64 on the rest. It never uses more. The three QV circuits where V2 is
  5721	  at 64 are the three weakest results in the corpus, and they are also the three
  5722	  that spill — see §14.5.
